{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791656259,"nonce":"5PXC+okh89Y4RWC14RWHVK9xfpI=","message":"Two read-only reviews of the slice 2 branch found defects the gates had not. Fixed on hot-reload-classes in 5b9bc3ca, 94a57521, c1c70153, e48e6f45 and e45d88c1; each of the first two was reproduced before it was fixed.\n\nFixed:\n- A frame that began before a reload panicked on an index when it called a method of an added class through a structural type (CallMethod on a virtual, VirtualClosure): both read the function and types of the program the frame began with. The class cases now make that call from main.\n- The setup of a new class was cut out of the entry function by data dependence alone. A static whose first value an inline test picks (`static var on = x == null`) took whichever arm was written last, and a store made under a test was made without it, silently. Any setup op inside a jump is refused now (\"the setup of the new classes has control flow in it\").\n- A setup that threw was never tried again, because the next reload took the class for one that was already running. The types from the first one not set up count as new until a setup runs to its end.\n- The scans of the closures a body hands to native code were not cleared by a reload.\n\nChecked after the fixes: Mac lib tests, the CLI tests, hybrid conformance 1069/1069, test_hot_reload.sh, parity and stdlib matrices; NUC lib tests (the one test that builds a wasm32 TargetMachine segfaults there, as before, and is skipped) and hot_reload 10/10; ashui fixtures v3, v4, v5, v6 under the default tiers, --jit-threshold 1, cranelift and llvm where v5 and v6 were run.\n\nFound and left, none reproduced:\n- Another thread can see the new program for as long as init_constants takes, before the new string literals are filled in. It needs a hybrid program with several Haxe threads running compiled code through a reload.\n- A new literal reuses the slot of a dropped constant of the same type, so a live object of a dropped class, or a dropped closure, reads the new text. The docs say so.\n- tiered.sigs and gate_checked survive for live beads, so a function whose parameter kinds changed is promoted again with the old marshaling signature.\n- stage_reload keeps an older staged program when a later save is refused.\n- Globals the loader cannot classify match by position among globals of the same type.","files":null}]}